  "reason": "Evidence: RNA multiprofile with scvi_n200 + transformer aggregation is the strongest configuration found (config_006, acc 0.653), while image-only models are very weak (best: imagenet_vit_l at 0.227). No multimodal configuration has been tested yet, so it is entirely unclear whether adding the weak image signal to the strong RNA signal helps, is neutral, or is harmful. Question: config_038 (multimodal, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, transformer, concat) directly isolates the effect of adding the image modality to the best-known RNA setup, using the slightly stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l > resnet50) and the simpler concat fusion as a baseline. Comparing config_038 to config_006 (0.653) tells us whether multimodal fusion adds value at all. Why this is the best next experiment: it answers the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact design question (should we include image data?) while keeping all other choices at their best-supported settings, making the comparison clean and interpretable under a limited budget."
}

